  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Is Dunbar an official City of Vancouver area?",
      "a": "The City's local area is \"Dunbar-Southlands,\" one of its 22 distinct areas, pairing the Dunbar house streets with Southlands and the Musqueam land at the south edge; \"Dunbar\" is the board / site name for the residential core.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "Which schools are located in Dunbar-Southlands?",
      "a": "On the VSB list: Kitchener Elementary (3455 West King Edward Avenue), Queen Elizabeth Elementary (4102 West 16th Avenue) and Southlands Elementary (5351 Camosun Street), with Kerrisdale Elementary (5555 Carnarvon Street) also listed under the Dunbar-Southlands heading; catchments are address-based, so check the exact address in the VSB locator.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "Is there a SkyTrain station in Dunbar?",
      "a": "No — Dunbar is bus-served, with route 7 running the Dunbar Street corridor between Nanaimo Station and the Dunbar loop, and east-west routes serving UBC and downtown.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "What makes Southlands different from the rest of Dunbar?",
      "a": "The City describes Southlands as a unique urban-country neighbourhood inside Dunbar-Southlands, beside the Musqueam First Nation land, in an area inhabited by Indigenous peoples as early as 400 B.C. and farmed since the 1800s.",
      "gen": "muse"
    }
  ]
